To implement a basic search algorithm for an ArrayList of Strings in Java, we can use a linear search approach. The algorithm iterates through each element in the ArrayList, comparing it to the target string using the equalsIgnoreCase() method to make the search case-insensitive. We also add a null check to handle null values in the ArrayList.

The final algorithm returns the index of the target string if found, or -1 if not found. The time complexity of this approach is O(n), making it suitable for small to medium-sized lists.

Here is the complete Java method:
```java
public int searchArrayList(ArrayList<String> list, String target) {
    for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {
        if (list.get(i)!= null && list.get(i).equalsIgnoreCase(target)) {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```
